    "name": "Crown of Witchcraft",
    "system": {
        "baseItem": null,
        "bulk": {
            "value": 0
        },
        "containerId": null,
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>An elegant accoutrement for a witch who has come into the higher echelons of power, a <em>crown of witchcraft</em> typically looks like a garland of flowering twigs, a jeweled circlet, or a tall hat of fine fabric. You gain a +1 item bonus to Intimidation checks, and if you're a witch, you gain a +2 item bonus to your patron skill.</p>\n<p>If you have a familiar, you can attach a small portion of the crown's material to your familiar, such as a strip of fabric from a hat tied around its tail or a sprig of natural material linked to its collar; the familiar doesn't need to invest the item itself. If you do this, your familiar gains the tough pet ability as long as the crown is invested by you.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Defiant Hex</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">F</span> (concentrate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> Gain 1 Focus Point, which you can spend only to cast a witch hex spell. If you don't spend this point by the end of this turn, it is lost.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Craft Requirements</strong> You are a witch.</p>"
        },
